-- title:
--   Vanishing on the supersingular locus lowers the weight by p-1
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $p \ge 5$, an algebraically closed field $K$ of characteristic $p$, and a natural number $N \ge 1$ whose image in $K$ is nonzero; fix an integer $k$ with $k \ge p+2$. Let $\varphi$ be a power series over $K$ belonging to [`ModPForms.modPMod N k K`](def/CuspForm_ModPForms.html#L12), the $K$-subspace of $K[[q]]$ spanned by those series $\mathrm{mk}\,(n \mapsto a_n \bmod p)$ arising from a modular form $f$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ whose $q$-expansion coefficients $\mathrm{qCoeff}\,f\,n$ are all integers $a_n$. Assume further that $\mathrm{resQFun}\,p\,N\,K\,hp5\,k\,\varphi$ vanishes identically on the index type $\mathrm{SSIndex}\,p\,N\,K\,hp5\,k$: that is, for a choice $G$ of element of the modular function field $K(\bar\jmath, \bar\jmath_N) \subset K((q))$ (the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldC` generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`) with $G = \varphi \cdot \theta(\bar\jmath)^{-\lfloor k/2\rfloor}$ as Laurent series, where $\theta$ is $q\,d/dq$ and $\bar\jmath = q^{-1}\cdot(\text{reduction of } \mathrm{jNum})$, each index $x$ has $\mathrm{lead}$ equal to $0$, i.e. the place $x_1$ evaluates $u^{a}G$ to $0$, where $u$ is the chosen uniformiser at $x_1$ and $a = \mathrm{poleOrder}$ is the integer $\lfloor \lfloor k/2\rfloor(\mathrm{jWidth} - 1)/\mathrm{placeWidth}\rfloor$ attached to $x$. The conclusion is that $\varphi$ already lies in [`ModPForms.modPMod N (k - ((p:ℤ) - 1)) K`](def/CuspForm_ModPForms.html#L12).
--
--   This is the divisibility step in Edixhoven's analysis of the weight filtration: a mod-$p$ form of weight $k \ge p+2$ whose leading values at the supersingular places all vanish is divisible by the Hasse invariant, hence lies in the space of weight $k-(p-1)$ (the two spaces being compared inside $K[[q]]$, since the Hasse invariant has $q$-expansion $1$). It supplies the exactness at the residue map for the supersingular datum constructed in [`ModPForms.nonempty_ssDatum_algebraicClosure`](thm.html#ModPForms.nonempty_ssDatum_algebraicClosure).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_SSHeckeV2_mem_modPMod_sub_of_resQFun_eq_zero.lean

